<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chronicle of Chicxulub</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Chronicle of Nakuk Pech</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chronicle of Chicxulub is an account of the Spanish conquest of Yucatán written in the Yucatec Maya language by Nakuk Pech, a noble of the Ceh Pech province, in the mid-16th century. It records the arrival of the Spaniards and presents the Pech lords as early allies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-montejo">Francisco de Montejo</a>, partly to secure their privileges under Spanish rule. It is one of the few native-written sources on the conquest.</p></div>
